== Dough ==

Preheat the oven to 350°F. 

Line two #cookie sheets{} with parchment paper or silicon baking mats. Set them aside.

In a #small mixing bowl{}, cream together the @salted butter{1/2%cup}(softened), @cream cheese{8%oz}(softened), and @milk{1/4%cup} until smooth.

Then, add in the @sugar{1.5%cups}, @vanilla extract{1%tbsp}, and @eggs{2}. Mix again to combine well.

In a separate #large bowl{}, combine the @flour{2.5%cups}, @cocoa powder{1/3%cup}, @sea salt{1%pinch}, and @baking powder{1%tsp}. Whisk the dry ingredients together.

Add the dry ingredients to the wet ingredients, a bit at a time, mixing well after each addition.

Next, fold in the @mini chocolate chips{2/3%cup} and @regular chocolate chips{1/4%cup}.

Use a medium-sized cookie scoop to scoop the dough out into round balls of dough. Arrange 12 cookies onto each of your prepared cookie sheets.

Wet your hands slightly and gently press down the tops of the cookies. Tap the cookie dough balls with your fingers to smooth the edges. Top with additional @?regular chocolate chips{} as desired.

Proceed to place the baking sheet in the oven and bake for ~{12-14%minutes}. Allow the cookies to cool on the baking sheet for ~{5%minutes} before transferring them to a wire cooling rack.

== Chocolate drizzle ==

In a small bowl, measure out @?regular chocolate chips{1/4%cup} and microwave for ~{1%minute} and allow to rest for ~{2%minutes} in the microwave before gently stirring. If necessary, heat for an additional ~{10-15%seconds} to fully melt.

Using a small spoon, drizzle the chocolate over the top of the baked cookies. Alternatively, you can transfer the chocolate to a small baggie and snip the corner to easily pipe the chocolate over the tops of the cookies.

Let cool to set for ~{5-10%minutes}, then serve and enjoy.